index 000000000..4730fd988
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/m1max-moe/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# M1 Max Qwen3.5-122B-A10B MoE benchmark harness
+
+Reproducible measurement for the mmap/MoE lazy-loading question analysed in
+`docs/local-m1max-qwen35moe.md`. Nothing here runs the model unless you set
+`RUN=1`; the drivers are guarded so the files can be read and edited safely.
+
+## Files
+
+- `common.sh`  - shared config (model path, ctx, threads, prompt). Edit here.
+- `monitor.sh` - background sampler: per-process RSS + system wired/compressed/
+  swap/pageins every 0.5 s. Captures the residency-set wiring that RSS alone misses.
+- `run_one.sh` - one llama-cli config, monitored, with a watchdog; appends a row
+  to `results/summary.tsv` (load ms, pp t/s, tg t/s, peak RSS, peak wired, swap).
+- `matrix.sh`  - the strategy matrix (guarded). `RUN=1 ./matrix.sh`.
+- `bench_throughput.sh` - clean pp/tg via llama-bench, JSON (guarded).
+
+## What it measures and why
+
+The core unknown is whether the resident expert working set stays under the
+~24-26 GiB budget, or grows toward all 33 GiB (forced swap). Three default
+mechanisms force full residency; the matrix isolates each:
+
+- `residency off` sets `GGML_METAL_NO_RESIDENCY=1` (stop Metal wiring the whole map)
+- `warmup off` sets `--no-warmup` (stop the all-256-expert warmup pass)
+- `ncmoe N` moves experts of the first N layers to a CPU buffer (lazy, unwired)
+
+## Running (only after the user says go)
+
+    RUN=1 ./matrix.sh                 # full matrix
+    RUN=1 ONLY=A_noresid ./matrix.sh  # one row
+    RUN=1 ./bench_throughput.sh       # throughput cross-check
+
+For a true cold-start load-time number, purge the page cache first (needs sudo):
+`sudo purge`. Without it, a second run reads a warm cache and load time is optimistic.
+
+## Reading results
+
+`results/summary.tsv` is tab-separated; `matrix.sh` prints it column-aligned at
+the end. Key reads: `peakWired_mb` near total RAM => whole model wired (bad);
+`maxSwap_mb` / `swapins_d` growth => thrashing; `tg_tps` >= 5 meets the goal.
+
+## Not yet covered (phase 2)
+
+Distinct-expert-over-time (does the hot set saturate under budget?) needs router
+instrumentation - a separate small patch, decided after these baselines exist.
